# Dry-run output is synthetic and carries no scientific weight — never committed.
*-dryrun.json

# Real experiment results ARE committed. That is the point of the record.
# Do not add results/ here.

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.Python
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
env/

.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# Raw sample caches ARE tracked. Excluding them was an audit hole: treatment
# draws existed on disk, untracked, while arguments that could void the run were
# being committed. The norm's whole value is that git proves temporal ordering,
# and it cannot prove it about a file git does not see.

# Local automation: the loop, the watcher and the Telegram notifier run on
# the maintainer's own machine. They are operational tooling, not part of the
# science, and the notifier is bound to one person's chat. Kept out of the
# public tree deliberately; no credential was ever in these files -- the token
# is read from the environment and is redacted from the module's own errors.
automation/
